  "conservation_statement": "This intricately worked cup is largely formed from small pieces of sheet silver, hammered into shape and joined with solder. The surfaces were then chased to create much of the decoration and to disguise the seams. The sash at the figure's waist and the lock of hair were noted in an examination from 1994 to be separately cast pieces attached with small tangs inserted through openings in the silver. X-ray fluorescence analysis of the silver in 1999 showed the composition to be 98.4% silver, 1.1% copper, 0.2% gold, and .04% lead by weight. The silver is protected by a surface coating of cellulose nitrate lacquer to reduce the formation of silver oxidation products.",
